   158	    Rule:
   159	    - Every non-legend pixel of a learned source color receives a translated copy
   160	      of the whole shared template, recolored to that rule's target color, with
   161	      the rule's anchor mapped onto the source pixel.
   162	    - The colored legend pairs themselves disappear, but the original shared teal
   163	      component stays in place and is recolored cell-by-cell by the target color
   164	      of the nearest rule anchor.
   165	    - Uninvolved bystander pixels remain unchanged.
   166	
   167	    Key insight: The local color pairs teach both the source->target mapping and
   168	    which anchor point inside the shared teal shape belongs to that rule; those
   169	    anchors partition the original template in place while also controlling how
   170	    the same whole shape is aligned when copied onto scattered source pixels.
